IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ssc-core`
IMPORT `ssc-seat`
IMPORT `ssc-definitions`
IMPORT `ssc8-sch4`

§ `Fixtures -- data only, no rules`

`fx person` MEANS Person WITH
    `date of birth` IS Date 1 1 1990
    `sex` IS Woman
    `marital status` IS `neither married nor in a civil partnership`
    `date of attaining pensionable age` IS Date 1 1 2056

`fx employment` MEANS Employment WITH
    `the employee` IS `fx person`
    `the kind of employer` IS `a company or other body corporate`
    `the employment began on` IS Date 1 1 2020
    `the employment ended on` IS NOTHING
    `held under a contract of service` IS TRUE
    `held in an office` IS FALSE
    `carried on in Great Britain` IS TRUE

`fx employment in Northern Ireland` MEANS Employment WITH
    `the employee` IS `fx person`
    `the kind of employer` IS `a company or other body corporate`
    `the employment began on` IS Date 1 1 2020
    `the employment ended on` IS NOTHING
    `held under a contract of service` IS TRUE
    `held in an office` IS FALSE
    `carried on in Great Britain` IS FALSE

`fx business` MEANS Employment WITH
    `the employee` IS `fx person`
    `the kind of employer` IS `an individual`
    `the employment began on` IS Date 1 1 2020
    `the employment ended on` IS NOTHING
    `held under a contract of service` IS FALSE
    `held in an office` IS FALSE
    `carried on in Great Britain` IS TRUE

`fx office` MEANS Employment WITH
    `the employee` IS `fx person`
    `the kind of employer` IS `a government department, public authority or other body of persons`
    `the employment began on` IS Date 1 1 2020
    `the employment ended on` IS NOTHING
    `held under a contract of service` IS FALSE
    `held in an office` IS TRUE
    `carried on in Great Britain` IS TRUE

`fx tax year` MEANS `Tax year` WITH `calendar year in which it begins` IS 2024

`fx limits` MEANS `Earnings limits` WITH
    `the tax year` IS `fx tax year`
    `lower earnings limit` IS 123
    `primary threshold` IS 242
    `upper earnings limit` IS 967
    `secondary threshold` IS 96

`fx tax week` MEANS `Tax week` WITH
    `the tax year` IS `fx tax year`
    `number of the week in the year` IS 10

GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `Earnings paid`
`fx paid` MEANS `Earnings paid` WITH
    `the amount in pounds` IS x
    `the tax week they were paid in` IS `fx tax week`

GIVEN y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Tax year`
`fx ty` MEANS `Tax year` WITH `calendar year in which it begins` IS y

GIVEN a IS A DATE, b IS A DATE
GIVETH A Period
`fx period` MEANS Period WITH
    `the first day` IS a
    `the last day` IS b

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A Person
`fx person attaining pensionable age on` MEANS Person WITH
    `date of birth` IS Date 1 1 1950
    `sex` IS Woman
    `marital status` IS `neither married nor in a civil partnership`
    `date of attaining pensionable age` IS d

GIVEN d IS A DATE, s IS A Sex
GIVETH A Person
`fx person born` MEANS Person WITH
    `date of birth` IS d
    `sex` IS s
    `marital status` IS `neither married nor in a civil partnership`
    `date of attaining pensionable age` IS Date 1 1 2056

GIVEN y IS A NUMBER, u IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `Earnings limits`
`fx limits for` MEANS `Earnings limits` WITH
    `the tax year` IS `fx ty` y
    `lower earnings limit` IS 1
    `primary threshold` IS 2
    `upper earnings limit` IS u
    `secondary threshold` IS 3

§ `Assertions`

#ASSERT `s 1(6)(a) the person is liable to pay a Class 1, Class 1A, Class 1B or Class 2 contribution` `Class 2` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- S2 s 1(6)(a) [L28]: no liability without the prescribed conditions
#ASSERT `s 1(6)(b) the person is entitled to pay Class 3 contributions` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- S3 s 1(6)(b) [L30]: no entitlement to pay Class 3 without the conditions
#ASSERT `s 1(6)(c) the person is entitled to pay a Class 1, Class 1A, Class 1B or Class 2 contribution` `Class 1 primary` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- S4 s 1(6)(c) [L31]: not liable and no regulations permitting: not entitled to pay
#ASSERT `s 2(1)(a) the person is an employed earner` `fx employment` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- S6 s 2(1)(a) [L35]: gainfully employed in GB under a contract of service
#ASSERT `s 2(1)(a) the person is an employed earner` `fx employment in Northern Ireland` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- S7 s 2(1)(a) [L35]: employed only in Northern Ireland: not an employed earner (the definition says in Great Britain)
#ASSERT `s 2(1)(b) the person is a self-employed earner` `fx business` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- S8 s 2(1)(b) [L36]: gainfully employed in GB otherwise than in employed earner's employment (the also-employed limb cannot be put: one Employment record)
#ASSERT `s 2(5) the person is treated as a self-employed earner as respects the week` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- S9 s 2(5) [L47]: self-employed for part of the week: so treated for the week
#ASSERT `s 2(3) the person is treated as an employed earner for all purposes of this Act` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- S11 s 2(3) [L45]: treated by reference to one employment: treated for all purposes
#ASSERT `s 3(1)(a) the payment is earnings` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- S12 s 3(1)(a) [L50]: a customer's tip paid direct to the worker: includes is not closed, so NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 4(1)(a) the sum is treated as remuneration derived from employed earner's employment` `statutory sick pay` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- S14 s 4(1)(a)(i) [L64-65]: SSP paid in satisfaction of entitlement
#ASSERT `s 4(1)(b) the sickness payment is treated as remuneration derived from employed earner's employment` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- S15 s 4(1)(b) [L73-75]: secondary contributor has made or remains liable to make payments
